---
import '../styles/style.css';
import '../styles/themes.css';
import '../styles/themes-generated.css';
const base = (import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, '')) + '/';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Serif:wght@300;400&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@300;400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@300;400;500;700&family=Inter:wght@300;400;700;900&family=VT323&family=Playfair+Display:wght@400;700;900&family=Orbitron:wght@400;700;900&family=Cormorant+Garamond:wght@300;400;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Source+Serif+4:wght@300;400&family=Archivo+Black&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <title>Side Channel Cloud</title>
  <script is:inline>
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme = localStorage.getItem('scc-theme') || 'amodo-dark';
  </script>
</head>
<body data-base={base}>
  <div class="page-frame"></div>
  <div class="progress" id="progress"></div>

  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="brand"><span class="glyph"></span> <b>SIDE&nbsp;CHANNEL</b> <span>// CLOUD</span></div>
    <nav class="navlinks">
      <a href={base} class="active" data-n="01">Landing</a>
      <a href={base + 'gallery/'} data-n="02">Dev Model Picker</a>
      <a href={base + 'explorer/'} data-n="03">Explorer</a>
      <a href="https://amododesign.com/" class="ext" data-n="//">Amodo Design</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <!-- pinned right column: wireframe + (during the hero) the access card -->
  <div class="scroll-stage stage-dim" id="stage">
    <canvas id="stage-canvas"></canvas>
    <div class="readout">
      DEV MODEL · <b data-model-name>—</b> <a id="ro-change" href={base + 'gallery/'}>change ↗</a><br>
      DIMS ······ <b data-model-dims>—</b><br>
      SUBSYSTEM · <b id="ro-sub">all</b><br>
      VIEW ······ <b id="ro-mode">ASSEMBLY</b> · SCROLL <b id="ro-pct">0%</b>
    </div>
    <div class="titleblock">
      SCC-HW · REV A<br>
      UNITS mm · SCALE NTS<br>
      THIRD-ANGLE PROJECTION
    </div>

    <aside class="access-card show" id="access-card">
      <span class="tag">Early access</span>
      <h3>Register your interest</h3>
      <p>Hardware lands in waves. Tell us what you need and we'll hold a slot
         in the next one.</p>
      <form id="access-form">
        <label>Name
          <input type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" required />
        </label>
        <label>Work email
          <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required />
        </label>
        <label>Company
          <input type="text" name="company" autocomplete="organization" />
        </label>
        <label>I need
          <select name="need">
            <option>A whole NVL72 rack</option>
            <option>Individual trays</option>
            <option>Telemetry / side-channel access</option>
            <option>Not sure yet</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <button class="cta-btn" type="submit">Get Access Today →</button>
      </form>
      <div class="access-success">
        <h3>You're on the list.</h3>
        <p>We'll be in touch when the next hardware wave opens. Meanwhile,
           pick the dev model you want to work against.</p>
        <a class="btn" href={base + 'gallery/'}>Open the Dev Model Picker →</a>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <!-- scrolling copy on the left -->
  <main class="scroll-content">

    <section class="section hero" data-stage="form" data-tags="" data-xray="false">
      <span class="tag">Bare-metal GPU · physical-layer telemetry</span>
      <h1>Rent the rack.<br><em>Read the side channels.</em></h1>
      <p>Side Channel Cloud provisions whole racks and trays — not virtual slices.
         Every system ships with instrumented access to its power rails, coolant
         loop and interconnect fabric, exposed as first-class telemetry.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn" href={base + 'gallery/'}>Dev Model Picker →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section explainer" data-stage="hidden" data-tags="" data-xray="false">
      <div class="explainer-card">
        <span class="tag">01 — Why we exist</span>
        <h2>We make infrastructure<br>to enable science.</h2>
        <p>There is a gap between the people thinking about AI security and the
           hardware it all runs on. We want more people working on AI security
           and verification — on real machines, with the side channels exposed,
           not behind a hypervisor. Side Channel Cloud is that bench: bare-metal
           racks and trays with rail-level power, coolant-loop and fabric
           telemetry as first-class outputs.</p>
        <div class="refs">
          <span class="refs-label">The reading that motivates this — RAND papers &amp; substacks</span>
          <a class="ref rand" href="https://www.rand.org/pubs/research_reports/RRA2849-1.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>RAND</b><span>Securing AI Model Weights · RR-A2849</span></a>
          <a class="ref rand" href="https://www.rand.org/pubs/working_papers/WRA3056-1.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>RAND</b><span>Hardware-Enabled Governance Mechanisms · WR-A3056</span></a>
          <a class="ref cnas" href="https://www.cnas.org/publications/reports/secure-governable-chips" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>CNAS</b><span>Secure, Governable Chips</span></a>
          <a class="ref arxiv" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.16074" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>arXiv</b><span>2408.16074 · Verification for international AI agreements</span></a>
          <a class="ref substack" href="https://importai.substack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>Substack</b><span>Import AI — Jack Clark</span></a>
          <a class="ref substack" href="https://www.hyperdimensional.co/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>Substack</b><span>Hyperdimensional — Dean Ball</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" data-tags="gpu,cpu,memory" data-xray="false">
      <span class="tag">02 — Compute</span>
      <h2>One NVLink domain,<br><em>72 GPUs</em>.</h2>
      <p>A GB200 NVL72 rack carries 18 compute trays, each with two Grace-Blackwell
         superchips: 72 Blackwell GPUs and 36 Grace CPUs sharing 13.5 TB of HBM3e
         behind a single NVLink-5 domain. You get the whole rack, or individual
         trays, on bare metal.</p>
      <div class="kv">
        <div><div class="n">72 / 36</div><div class="l">GPU / Grace CPU</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">13.5 TB</div><div class="l">HBM3e per rack</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">18× 1U</div><div class="l">compute trays</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="refs">
        <span class="refs-label">Further reading</span>
        <a class="ref arxiv" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.11341" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>arXiv</b><span>2303.11341 · Catching a Chinchilla — compute monitoring</span></a>
        <a class="ref rand" href="https://www.rand.org/pubs/working_papers/WRA3056-1.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>RAND</b><span>Hardware-Enabled Governance Mechanisms</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" data-tags="coldplate,tube,manifold" data-xray="true">
      <span class="tag">03 — Side channels</span>
      <h2>The <em>coolant loop</em>,<br>instrumented.</h2>
      <p>Direct-to-chip cold plates on every superchip, blind-mate quick disconnects
         at the tray rear, and dual vertical manifolds carrying the rack loop.
         We expose per-plate inlet/outlet temperature, flow rate and pressure delta
         at one-second resolution.</p>
      <div class="kv">
        <div><div class="n">D2C</div><div class="l">cold plate per chip</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">2×</div><div class="l">rack manifolds</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">1 s</div><div class="l">sample interval</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="refs">
        <span class="refs-label">Further reading</span>
        <a class="ref conf" href="https://www.usenix.org/conference/usenixsecurity15/technical-sessions/presentation/masti" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>USENIX</b><span>Thermal covert channels on multi-core (Sec '15)</span></a>
        <a class="ref conf" href="https://blog.trailofbits.com/2024/01/16/leftoverlocals-listening-to-llm-responses-through-leaked-gpu-local-memory/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>ToB</b><span>LeftoverLocals — leaked GPU local memory</span></a>
        <a class="ref rand" href="https://www.rand.org/pubs/research_reports/RRA2849-1.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>RAND</b><span>Securing AI Model Weights · RR-A2849</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" data-tags="nic,interconnect,connector,cable" data-xray="true">
      <span class="tag">04 — Network</span>
      <h2>NVLink counters,<br><em>per link</em>.</h2>
      <p>Nine NVLink switch trays sit mid-rack, joined to every compute tray through
         a rear copper cable cartridge. Per-port bandwidth, replay and CRC error
         counters are exported for the full 130 TB/s domain — observability that
         normally ends at the cage door.</p>
      <div class="kv">
        <div><div class="n">130 TB/s</div><div class="l">NVLink-5 domain</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">9× 1U</div><div class="l">switch trays</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">1.8 TB/s</div><div class="l">per GPU</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="refs">
        <span class="refs-label">Further reading</span>
        <a class="ref conf" href="https://www.vusec.net/projects/netcat/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>S&P</b><span>NetCAT — network cache attacks (S&P '20)</span></a>
        <a class="ref conf" href="https://www.cs.ucr.edu/~nael/pubs/ccs18.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>CCS</b><span>Rendered Insecure — practical GPU side channels (CCS '18)</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" data-tags="power,busbar" data-xray="true">
      <span class="tag">05 — Power</span>
      <h2>Rail-level<br><em>power metering</em>.</h2>
      <p>Six power shelves rectify to a 48 V DC busbar running the height of the
         rack; each tray blind-mates onto it. We meter every shelf, every busbar
         tap and every VRM domain, so you can attribute watts to workloads and
         catch a degrading phase before it throttles you.</p>
      <div class="kv">
        <div><div class="n">48 V</div><div class="l">DC busbar</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">≈120 kW</div><div class="l">rack budget</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">6×</div><div class="l">power shelves</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="refs">
        <span class="refs-label">Further reading</span>
        <a class="ref conf" href="https://www.hertzbleed.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>USENIX</b><span>Hertzbleed — power into remote timing (Sec '22)</span></a>
        <a class="ref conf" href="https://platypusattack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>S&P</b><span>PLATYPUS — software power side channels (S&P '21)</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" data-tags="connector,busbar,tube" data-xray="true">
      <span class="tag">06 — Taps</span>
      <h2>Physical <em>taps</em>,<br>by design.</h2>
      <p>Every blind-mate interface in the rack is a sanctioned probe point: busbar
         taps for current waveforms, QD ports for loop sensing, NVLink cartridge
         connectors for fabric capture, and BMC/debug headers on every tray. Bring
         a scope, a logic analyser, or our interposers — the access is contractual,
         not adversarial.</p>
      <div class="kv">
        <div><div class="n">3+</div><div class="l">tap classes / tray</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">BMC</div><div class="l">out-of-band, yours</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">scope-ready</div><div class="l">probe fixtures</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="refs">
        <span class="refs-label">Further reading</span>
        <a class="ref arxiv" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.16074" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>arXiv</b><span>2408.16074 · Verification for international AI agreements</span></a>
        <a class="ref cnas" href="https://www.cnas.org/publications/reports/secure-governable-chips" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>CNAS</b><span>Secure, Governable Chips</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="provision" data-tags="" data-xray="false">
      <span class="tag">07 — Provision</span>
      <h2>Tray or rack.<br><em>Yours in minutes.</em></h2>
      <p>Pick your dev model from the picker — GB200 NVL72, DGX H100, or PCIe —
         register your interest above, and get bare-metal access plus the full
         telemetry feed when your wave opens.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn" href={base + 'gallery/'}>Open the Dev Model Picker →</a>
        <a class="btn" href="#top" onclick="window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'});return false;">Get Access Today ↑</a>
      </div>
      <div class="refs">
        <span class="refs-label">Further reading</span>
        <a class="ref arxiv" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.11341" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>arXiv</b><span>2303.11341 · Compute monitoring</span></a>
        <a class="ref arxiv" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.16074" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>arXiv</b><span>2408.16074 · Treaty verification methods</span></a>
        <a class="ref substack" href="https://importai.substack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b>Substack</b><span>Import AI</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/scroll-site.js';
  </script>
</body>
</html>
